  "answer": "LIWC is incorporated into the system as part of the PTSD detection baseline model. It is used alongside unigram and character n-gram language models to classify tweets for PTSD detection. Specifically, the system calculates the proportion of tweets scored positively by each LIWC category, and these proportions are used as a feature vector in a loglinear regression model. This approach allows the system to analyze mental health through Twitter data by leveraging LIWC's categorical analysis capabilities [E3][E4].",
